<Concept title="Reyburn and Octo Diablo" section="States">
  <p>This contract supersedes the authored Reyburn and Octo attack/phase tables in
  /states/bosses. Source: psz-re 29266e6, ROM overlay 20/21 and the retained
  melonDS natural-damage captures. It defines the testable port; complete
  input/RNG/motion parity remains an open requirement.</p>
  <h2>Shared execution</h2>
  <p>DescriptorBoss MUST advance descriptor stages and events at 30 action ticks
  per second, preserving catch-up ticks. Damage windows MUST use their original
  frame boundaries, persist hit memory until closing, and close on cancellation.
  Damage MUST NOT replace boss actions with generic flinch. Death MUST cancel all
  channels and projectiles, award completion once, and permit a fresh encounter.</p>
  <h2>Reyburn</h2>
  <p>The controller MUST use the sixteen recovered sequence identities. Budgets
  MUST initialize from the difficulty's base stat HP, separately from encounter
  HP. Positive-guarded budgets use rounded 819/4096 and 1638/4096. Part 1 spends
  the first; all hits spend the second. Source-bearing damage and hit counters
  MUST use an inclusive 0x2aaa turn threshold. Completion, not entry, clears the
  sequence-specific counters. Action 2 notification 0 MUST enable the modifier;
  changing HP alone MUST NOT enable it.</p>
  <p>Selection MUST preserve damage-priority order, spatial bands, the four-way
  fallback without reroll, and 375/1500/150 action-tick timers. Normal/advancing
  bites MUST run separate counts; breath MUST run 10 → 11 → 12 and release at
  notification 4, with nine-tick repeat spacing and a six-projectile pool.
  The three-shot fan MUST use heading ±0x0e38. Facing MUST remain locked during
  normal bite damage windows. Four hurt parts MUST share HP and hit ownership.</p>
  <h2>Octo Diablo</h2>
  <p>Mode 0 MUST clamp post-subtraction HP at integer half of encounter maximum,
  before death checks. Reaching half MUST latch a transition without interrupting
  an active attack. The boundary sequence MUST be 0 → 2 → 14 → 18 → 0;
  step 2 waits for limbs, step 14 withdraws/repositions, and mode changes before
  the latch clears. Body and six limb channels MUST advance independently.</p>
  <p>Spout MUST play 8 → 9 → 10 → 11 → 1; aim may hold action 9 for up to 30
  ticks, and action 10 notification 0 releases the projectile. Variant weights
  [90,0,10] and [0,90,10] MUST select projectiles, never the main attack.
  Main selection MUST retain ordered timer/hit-count checks. Limb hits MUST
  share encounter HP and receive their own reaction without cancelling body
  playback. Death MUST cancel every limb.</p>
  <h2>Parity boundaries and validation</h2>
  <p>Recovered timing, budgets and request priorities MUST be tested against
  retained emulator evidence and boundary inputs. A field probe MUST exercise
  both real arena spawns, clips, incoming damage, phase transition, projectiles,
  HUD, death, return warp and retry. Captured timing is not proof of full parity.
  Arena-relative placement, movement/root-motion approximation, unported capture
  ownership/escape input, attack-group damage/status/effects and multiplayer
  targeting MUST be disclosed until independently compared to the original.
  Scorecard grades MUST remain unchanged pending Kion's playtest.</p>
</Concept>
